      },
      "message": "feat(tools): multi-seat indexable face mills and end mills\n\nA cutter body (tool item) whose seats all take one shared insert\nresolves to the milling tool record: diameter, corner radius, flutes,\nflute length and centre cutting. The tool is never smaller than the\nreal cutter: below 90 degrees the cutting diameter is the edge reach,\nand the shank holds the rest of the inserts. In an assembly the seats\nmust put the cutting point on DC, and the judged body is enclosed.\n\nRefs #3646\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
