      "message": "fix(tools): check every seat, the real profile and one source in the multi-seat assembly\n\nThe #4192 review found three classes where the assembled cutter could\nbe smaller than the real one:\n\n- A body inside the cutting depth was checked against diameter/2. It is\n  now checked against the tool profile at the band's lowest point, the\n  corner arc included (bull-nose and round-insert cutters).\n- Only the mounted seat was checked. Each seat port of the body is now\n  placed as the mounted insert is and must be on DC, in the tip plane\n  and turned as the mounted seat. A seat count's seats are copies of the\n  one port.\n- The derived cutter was not bound to the mounted insert. The cutter now\n  keeps the body and insert it was derived from, and `assembled` takes\n  the assembly nodes and refuses another body or insert by name.\n\n`MillingCutter::assembled` moves to milling_cutter_assembly.rs and takes\n`&[AssemblyNode]`; nothing outside the module read it.\n\nRefs #3646\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
